# Photographs dropped in here are working files, never commits.
#
# The district folders beside this one are a staging area: put the originals
# in, whatever their size or format, and they get converted and uploaded to
# the R2 bucket. The site reads them from there, not from here — see
# src/lib/assets.ts.
#
# Without this rule a 3 MB original lands in git the first time someone runs
# `git add .`, and git keeps every version of a binary forever. That is
# already true of ~8 MB of hero video, which is exactly the mistake this
# folder should not repeat.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
# .jfif is what Windows saves a JPEG as when it comes out of a browser's
# right-click menu. It slipped past a jpg/jpeg rule on the first try.
*.jfif
*.png
*.webp
*.heic
*.heif
*.avif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp

# The map stays: README.md explains where the files actually go, and .gitkeep
# is what makes git carry the empty folders at all.
!README.md
!.gitkeep
